{
  "id": 450304321,
  "iid": 23403,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Qt: Enforce QMessageBox style with QProxyStyle instead of app stylesheet",
  "description": "Style sheets override the palette. They also end up disabling the\npropagation of ApplicationPaletteChange and PaletteChange events\nto children, and automatically forwarding palette changes to children.\n\nInstead of using a main application style sheet in order to change\nthe behavior of QMessageBox on all styles, use a QProxyStyle. This\nhas the advantage that palette changes are correctly forwarded to\nwidgets that don't have their own style sheet. Widgets with their\nown style sheet still need additional notification.\n\nThis addresses some of the cases in #20774 for widgets that don't\nhave style sheets, such as the status bar.\n\nPing commit 09c98896fe8ba549c7f396ced46e35b7d53255ac, which this\nre-implements but without the style sheet issues.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-01-29T03:21:39.979Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-29T12:15:14.898Z",
